          %title
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://particle-theory.physics.lsa.umich.edu/kane/"} Webpage
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordon_L._Kane"} Wikipedia entry
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Nature article,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.nature.com/news/particle-physics-is-at-a-turning-point-1.9675"} Particle physics is at a turning point
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.aps.org/programs/honors/prizes/prizerecipient.cfm?last_nm=Kane&first_nm=Gordon&year=2017"} Sakurai prize 2017
                “For instrumental contributions to the theory of the properties, reactions, and signatures of the Higgs boson.”
          %p
            On the history of the concept of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li#KaneShifman00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Supersymmetric World: The Beginnings of The Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/4611"} doi:10.1142/4611
              %ul
                %li#KaneShifman01
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                  %em Introduction to “The Supersymmetric world”
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0102298"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0102298
                  ), chapter in:
                  %a{:href => "#KaneShifman00"} Kane-Shifman 00
          %p
            Kane has been arguing that
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
            of the kind of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+particle"} Higgs particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            around 120-130 GeV. He stated this in
          %ul
            %li#Kane11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em String theory and generic predictions for our world – superpartner masses, LHC signatures, dark matter, EWSB, cosmological history of universe, etc
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://conferencing.uwex.edu/conferences/stringpheno2011/documents/kane.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            a few months before the actual detection of the Higgs particle (and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                  %mn 125
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim 125
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GeV"} GeV
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Piyush+Kumar"} Piyush Kumar
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higgs Mass Prediction for Realistic String/M Theory Vacua
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.1059"} arXiv:1112.1059
          %p
            a few days before the result was officially announced (a useful informed comment is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.columbia.edu/~woit/wordpress/?p=4262&cpage=1#comment-101525"} here
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From Planck-scale M-theory to predictions for superpartners at LHC, soon
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://agenda.albanova.se/getFile.py/access?contribId=278&resId=250&materialId=slides&confId=4682"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String/M-theories About Our World Are Testable in the traditional Physics Way
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.whytrustatheory2015.philosophie.uni-muenchen.de/index.html"} Why Trust a Theory? Reconsidering Scientific Methodology in Light of Modern Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.07511"} arXiv:1601.07511
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://videoonline.edu.lmu.de/en/node/7485"} video
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                %em
                  Compactifying M-theory on a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                  manifold to describe/explain our world – Predictions for LHC (gluinos, winos, squarks), and dark matter
                (
                %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/506172/contributions/2026001/attachments/1256948/1855957/CMS_talk.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Kane17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String theory and the real world
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://iopscience.iop.org/book/978-1-6817-4489-6"} doi:0.1088/978-1-6817-4489-6
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/book/978-0-7503-3583-6"} ISBN:978-0-7503-3583-6
            %li#Kane18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"}> Gordon Kane
                ,
                %em Exciting Implications of LHC Higgs Boson Data
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05199"}> arXiv:1802.05199
                )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+couplings"} Yukawa couplings
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
          %ul
            %li
              Eric Gonzalez,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"} Gordon Kane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcolm+Perry"} Malcolm Perry
              %em
                Quark and lepton mass matrices from localization in M-theory on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                orbifold
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.11820"}> arXiv:2002.11820
              )
          %p
            and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
            masses:
          %ul
            %li
              Eric Gonzalez,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Kane"} Gordon Kane
              %em Neutrino mass matrices from localization in M-theory on G₂ orbifold
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.12893"}> arXiv:2107.12893
              )
          %h2#related_lab_entries
            Related
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"}> M-theory on G₂-manifolds
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+field"}> Higgs field
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+stability"} vacuum stability
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/naturalness"} naturalness
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/people"} people
